 my three-step process so  that you can provide more value  and get paid what you're worth let's go  step number one is build your top 50  list think about who are the 50 people  that if they knew you if they liked you  if they trusted you if they respected  you  if they recognized who you were and and  knew what you were up to  that that would mean something right for  a lot of people  it doesn't matter if they know you or  not they're not going to be a referral  source they're not going to be a partner  for you  but who are the 50 people that matter  most that that  you would love to have as dream clients  or dream partnerships  build that list of 50 people that you  want to make contact with  step number two is be their chief goal  officer if you want to have success and  this isn't just for the 50 list but  for your clients for your team for your  relationships  be the person's chief goal officer when  you understand  not just what you want but what they  want and you help them get it  that's when the whole world opens up the  reason why i was able to get  to to work with tony robbins and his  team was  i made a video at the starting point  right i made a video that they liked  that  that put tony in a good light uh that  was respectful that  made him look as well as a as a business  guru  on top of everything else that he was  already doing and then  every interaction i had afterwards i'm  bringing them value i'm helping them  with their youtube channel helping  spread the awareness for  programs and courses that he has coming  up right i'm trying to be a  a resource for them but around things  that they care about  not the things that i want to talk about  it's what they care about and so if  you're following your 50 people  right you have your list of 50 pay  attention to what they're talking about  try to catch them when they're in a time  of need right so classic examples are  when somebody's pitching a book  or when they're pitching a new deal or  where they're trying to get eyeballs on  a new show that they just launched like  what are they talking about  if they've gone super dark and super  quiet and they're not active on any of  their social platforms  it's really hard to start to make an  entrance  one of the people on my list has just  gone dark and we've had a good  relationship with the past  two years and now he's gone dark he's in  book writing mode  it's like i'm in book writing mode now  and i'm not gonna surface for the next  four months  so i'm not gonna send him anything in  the next four months he's not gonna be  posting anything for the next four  months  there's no point in me reaching out and  seeing how he's doing the next four  months because he doesn't want to be  bothered  but when he resurfaces and comes up for  air you know what he's going to need  he's going to need promotion he's going  gonna need marketing he's gonna need  support you know who's gonna be there  this guy right like that's the process  if you  promote my book right now it just came  out i'm just in launch mode i'm trying  to get eyeballs on it right  if you promote my book right now if i'm  on your list i'm way more likely to  reshare your stuff  to share the post to pay attention to  who you are  than in two months if you did the same  thing and that's for everybody  everybody's going in these cycles  what do they care about most right now  what matters most to them right now  and then you finding a way to be a  resource to help them so that they know  who you are they recognize your name and  say  that person that person's awesome i love  that person  when you get to that point then when you  reach out with an ask when you say hey  i'd love if you could xyz  they're way more receptive to you  because of all the value that you've  brought  be their chief goal officer understand  what they want and help them get it  and then you can ask for what you want  and set number three is then just  constantly follow up with value where  most people  quit is they don't get an immediate  response the more  successful the person is that you're  chasing down the harder it's going to be  to reach them  the harder it's going to be to penetrate  them right so you have to consistently  follow through  right like just look again at my tony  robbins example took it took a while to  get that first interview  that got cancelled they promised to do  another one it took two years before  that next one happened  of of constantly following up right not  not every day but a couple times a month  constantly  sending some value pitching ideas  helping them with their youtube channel  always through tony's team to the point  where it's like this guy evan is  bringing us so much value  once tony's opening up his calendar  again we have to make a spot for him  right most people quit too soon would  you wait  you know a year to get the first thing  and then two years before it actually  happens right another two years would  you wait that long would you follow up  that much like if you're on a a short  timeline and that this business  has to work in six months and you're  gonna sell it to do something else  this isn't the strategy but if you're on  a lifelong path like these are people  who you want to work with these are  these are your heroes who you can't wait  to get in front of  then you have to follow through you got  to stay on it be their chief gold  officer but don't give up  after the first time if you're not  getting results right  if you dm me and i don't respond the  first time if you leave an amazing  comment and i don't see it like that's  gonna happen  you're gonna get lost in the shuffle a  lot of times and especially if you're  only doing it once  but if every time i go live on instagram  you're there  asking great questions showing love and  support when i went live on youtube  talking about  my book if you were there right asking  questions showing love to the people  if you bought the book and shared it  with your story right  i'm gonna notice you and and forget  about me maybe  you know who cares about me great the  next person gary vee or tony robbins or  kevin hart or will smith  or oprah whoever the person is that you  love the most  right your top 50 you're constantly  paying attention and at any given point  in time  not all 50 of them are going to need  something but  inevitably somebody on that list right  now needs something  they need help they need support they  need outreach they need marketing  they need exposure you can help be that  person for them  and then they're going to remember you  the constant never-ending  ongoing outreach of value to build the  business that you want to build  most entrepreneurs don't charge enough  you're so worried about getting rejected  or losing clients because of a higher  price  that you'll charge just enough so you  stay just above  their survival line that's not how  winning businesses are built  if you can't break your survival  mentality you'll stay in survival mode  forever  so the first brand deal that i ever got  was for 500  from a major telecommunications company  and they wanted me to write for their  website  and they hired me they hired nine other  people to write an  article and they said write 300 words  we'll pay you 500 bucks  and for me 500 bucks at the time i  thought this is great  it's amazing i got my first deal 500  bucks is cash  i'm pumped but more important i'm  getting a link from  a huge company and for anybody back in  the old school seo days  if you get linked from a big company  that can mean a lot for your business to  take off for rankings  so i would have done it for free just  for the link so they gave me the 500  bucks  but i didn't just write the 300 words  because i wanted to  give more value i wanted to get paid  based off the value that i could provide  and so i had to show them  here's how much value i can bring and so  instead of writing 300 words  i wrote 1500 words right five times more  than what they asked  and then i made a video talking about it  and then i also promoted it to my  newsletter list  promoted to my audience let people know  when that article came up  here it was and so what happened as a  result of me doing all this work  i was the only one doing it so when they  came to the end of the series  i had my posts that were crushing it and  then nine other people were doing what  was asked the 300 words  the bare minimum what is asked of you is  the bare minimum  that's your ticket into the door if you  just did what they asked that's not  enough  that's not giving them insane value and  so i was the only one that they hired  10 of us went in i was the only one who  kept going because i brought them way  more value  now i started charging more what i was  doing i went from 500 bucks  per post to a thousand to 1500 to 2000  kept increasing my prices because i was  bringing them the value and they could  see it  and so the very beginning i was grateful  i was just grateful to get the gig i was  grateful to get my first  corporate gig to get 500 bucks to get a  link from the website i was grateful i  was pumped i was i was happy i was  excited this is the best  but i wanted to make this a business and  you can't have a business on 500 bucks a  month  and so i had to ask myself how do i  bring more value if i want to get paid  more  i need to bring more value and either  these guys are going to recognize it  or somebody else will i'm going to give  you a three-step process  you can use to start charging more step  number one is give the baker's dozen  i don't know how common a term this is  but i remember when i was young growing  up at my  at my cottage we'd always go to this  local bake shop and they sold donuts  and they would sell a 12 pack of donuts  but they would add a 13th one in for  free and they called it the baker's  dozen a dozen is supposed to be 12  but they give you a 13th donut for free  so you get your 12 and you can pick one  more  for free as a bonus as an extra as more  value  and so you want to think about that in  your business as well think about all  the clients that you're helping  how can you give the baker's dozen how  can you give that one extra donut that  one extra little bit of value  not of what you want to do but what is  actually valuable for them  right in the example of my client i  wrote five times as many words i added  the video  i promoted to my newsletter list think  about being your client's chief goal  officer  what are they trying to accomplish  they're hiring you for something but  they also have bigger goals in their  life or business  what are they trying to accomplish and  the more you can help them  accomplish that thing the more they're  going to love you the more they're going  to refer you and the more they're going  to pay you  for helping them out and so adopt the  baker's dozen mentality  you're just assuming that what is on  paper is not going to be enough  that that's just the entry point that's  the bare minimum you're always going to  add in that extra doughnut  step two increase your prices by 30  just try it for your next client  increase your prices 30  a big problem for a lot of entrepreneurs  is you're already doing the baker's  dozen you're doing more than the baker's  dozen you're given insane value you're  spending an incredible amount of time  researching helping thinking about your  client and you're just not getting paid  enough for it  and so your next client that comes in  just try  30 more 30 more 30 percent more  and you'll slowly transition to people  that have bigger clients  because only doing work with people who  can't afford to pay you what you're  worth  is not how you're going to build a great  business it's honestly better to work  with people who can afford to pay you  and then you keep 10 of your clients to  be charity cases  that's actually even for free you don't  charge them it's free  it's your it's your community service  it's your work to give back  to the the community around you amazing  but you can't build your business off of  that  most of your business has to be of  people who are paying you what you're  worth  and so the next client that comes in you  summon your courage  you look at your typical price that you  would charge now it's 30  more and step three is start small i  love starting small  i hate having to go into a business and  do this giant pitch because it's a six  figure deal  i hate that it takes too long it has to  go through too many  pains has to have too many meetings it's  a committee to make a decision  just takes too long the best place to  start is small  just find the smallest deal to get  started on one tiny little thing that  you can do for them  and then be the best supplier that  they've ever worked with  be the best supplier that they have ever  worked with and guess what's gonna  happen  they're gonna fight for ways to bring  you back in when i did that deal with  the telecommunications company  they loved me so much they fought for  ways to have me come back in they  they wanted me to speak at events they  wanted me to interview people for their  channel  they were looking for ways like can we  give this to evan can we have evan do  this  sort of as one throw away thing one 300  word article  became a three-year relationship  something like that it's crazy  i want that for you i don't want you to  have to go through crazy big proposals  it takes six months to get a decision  find one tiny little thing that you can  get started off  and then show the value that you bring  and then they're gonna fight over  themselves to have you do more work  they'll say can you do this  can you do that we have a problem here  can you help out here too and if it's in  your wheelhouse and you say yes  i'm happy to help and suddenly you get  more and more and more of the entire  business  without ever having to pitch without  ever having to present  because you're bringing so much value i  think most people are confused about  money  most people don't have a healthy  relationship with money  there are the people who think that  money is everything the money is the  only important thing in the world and  you need to chase it down and it's your  duty and responsibility and obligations  like it's number one  the person walking into my house and my  place of business that's my next suit  that's my next payment that's my next  whatever it's only focused on money  and there's other people who think money  is the root of all  evil and that money is a bad thing  money is a tool money helps you get a  lot of things done money helps you go  places money helps you accomplish your  mission  money needs to be in your top five it's  just not number one  money needs to be in your top five if  money does not become important at some  point to you if it's not in your top  five priorities you'll never make money  and you'll always be  by yourself struggling trying to figure  out how to make something work  but it's not number one either if you  put money above all else you'll end up  doing a lot of work that you hate and  you never get good at it just because  you're chasing opportunities  this is a big reason why so many  entrepreneurs fail  you're just chasing the hottest thing  for this year  that you don't have a passion or  interest in and then you lose because  the people who love that destroy you  when i first started doing this helping  entrepreneurs i never thought i was  going to make money  my first speaking gig my first option to  help people was in canada in my hometown  of toronto was at a ymca it was a free  event  they had an entrepreneurship program and  they asked me to come and speak to their  members  it was free i wasn't getting paid to do  it just wanted to help out i just sold  my business i wanted to give back  i was saying yes to everything i  actually didn't even know what i wanted  to do next  and so i show up and this is big room  full of chairs  and only three people show up to that  first event  only three people and as soon as i  walked in the room and i saw three  people my heart sank  i felt like i'm never gonna be able to  make anything from this if only three  people show up to a free event  how am i ever going to make money from  it i didn't know  but i gave my best to those three people  i know that i helped those three people  and had an impact on their lives  we then went for coffee afterwards and  continued the conversation i know  that i helped them and it filled my soul  and had to find a way to keep doing it  i knew i had to find a way to keep doing  it even if i never made money  and so i did i kept doing speaking gigs  i did my website  i did my youtube channel and slowly  slowly slowly slowly  it started to come in as i figured out  the second key  important piece which is figuring out  how to bring value to other people  when you find something that you love  doing and you combine it with how it  brings value to other people  that's when you start making money  if it's something that you just love  doing but nobody else likes it  there's zero value to anybody else you  have a hobby  you have a hobby if you're only chasing  stuff that people like and need  but you don't like doing it you're never  gonna get great at it  you might make a little bit of money but  you're never gonna get great at it  you're never gonna be  all time you're never gonna build a huge  business  and so is that combination of doing work  that you love doing  and mix it with where does an  opportunity that people need  it's a problem that you are solving mix  those things together  you have a super successful business if  you want to sign up for the entire  billionaire mindset series for free and  get the companion bonus pdf calendar  check the link right there next to me i  think you'll love it  continue to believe and i'll see you  there
 

